today is holocaust remembrance day it  was established by the united nations  so that we never forget the horrific  acts against the jewish people during  world war  ii bianca holman is live this morning at  the warsaw remembrance garden here in  the valley with more on this  bianca good morning hey good morning  john you know we've got a strong and  very active jewish community here in las  vegas  around more than 70 thousand people here  and the temple beth shalom they've been  in the community  for more than 70 years so a very strong  active community here and  here at the temple they have a  remembrance garden that remembrance  garden is named after the warsaw ghetto  in poland  now in 1940 more than 350 thousand jews  were exiled by german soldiers to a  small area  this area was enclosed by a 10-foot wall  with barbed wire and broken glass  dandelions are used to actually remember  the holocaust but the warsaw ghetto  remembrance garden here in las vegas is  a place to reflect on the atrocities  that occurred rabbi felipe goodman says  it's important to understand  why the holocaust happened  it happened because of basic prejudice  and racial bias and complete a lack of  tolerance to other human beings  and may i say that in america today with  the racial violence that we're seeing  we are always a step away to committing  horrible acts that could lead to  something like what happened to my  people  in the 40s in europe  there is a lot of education in our  public schools regarding the holocaust  susan dubin the holocaust resource  center library director tells me  they've got several training sessions  for teachers this spring and matter of  fact today there's a virtual visit to  the how did you survive  exhibit at the west charleston library  that exhibit is filled with stories from  holocaust survivors  and she also tells me we've got about  100 holocaust survivors here in southern  nevada  and if you'd like to attend that virtual  tour you must contact  susan dubin and her information is  listed on the holocaust resource  library website reporting live from town  center in  havenwood bianca holman 8 news now
 

